 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "bava_metzia.93b.20",
   "daf": "93b",
   "sentenceId": 19,
   "he": "הַלִּסְטִים – הֲרֵי זֶה אוֹנֶס. אַמַּאי? לוֹקֵי גַּבְרָא לַהֲדֵי גַּבְרָא! אָמַר רַב: בְּלִסְטִים מְזוּיָּין.",
   "en": "The mishna teaches that if «bandits came, this is» considered «a circumstance beyond one’s control.» The Gemara asks: «Why? Let one man stand against another man.» The shepherd should defend his flock and fight the bandit, as that is what he was hired to do. «Rav said:» The mishna is referring «to armed bandits,» against whom the shepherd cannot reasonably defend the flock."
  }
